   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "״זֶה גִּיטִּיךְ מֵהַיּוֹם, אִם מַתִּי מֵחוֹלִי זֶה״, וְעָמַד וְהָלַךְ בַּשּׁוּק כּוּ׳.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If one says to his wife: «This is your bill of divorce from today if I die from this illness,» and he recovered, «and he arose and walked in the market» and became ill again and died, then it must be assessed whether he died from the first illness and it is therefore a valid bill of divorce. But if he did not die from this illness then it is not a valid bill of divorce."
  }
